===Noun===
{{wp}}
[[File:Poids fonte 1 kg 02.jpg|thumb|Weight (3) for balance.]]
{{en-noun|~}}

# The downwards force an object experiences due to [[gravity]].
# An object used to make something [[heavier]].
# {{senseid|en|Q1320546}} A [[standardized]] block of [[metal]] used in a [[balance]] to measure the [[mass]] of another object.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[importance|Importance]] or [[influence]].
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=I liked the man for his own sake, and even had he promised to turn out a celebrity it would have had no '''weight''' with me. I look upon notoriety with the same indifference as on the buttons on a man's shirt-front, or the crest on his note-paper.}}
#* '''1907''' Alonso de Espinosa, Hakluyt Society & Sir Clements Robert Markham, ''The Guanches of Tenerife: the holy image of Our Lady of Candelaria, and the Spanish conquest and settlement,'' Printed for the Hakluyt Society, p116
#*: Another knight came to settle on the island, a man of much '''weight''' and position, on whom the Adelantados of all the island relied, and who was made a magistrate.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1945|author=Mikia Pezas|title=The price of liberty|publisher=I. Washburn, Inc.|page=11
|passage="You surely are a man of some '''weight''' around here," I said.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q65088374}} {{lb|en|exercise|weightlifting}} An object, such as a [[weight plate]] or [[barbell]], used for [[strength training]].
#: {{ux|en|He's working out with '''weights'''. Weight-bearing exercise is now understood to be just as important as cardio.}}
## {{senseid|en|Q117208690}} {{lb|en|sometimes|specifically}} {{ellipsis of|en|free weight<id:Q117208690>}}, as contrasted with the weights inside an exercise machine.
##: {{syn|en|black iron<id:Q117208690><qq:gym jargon>}}
##: {{ux|en|I prefer '''weights''' over machines.}}
# {{lb|en|lubricants}} [[viscosity|Viscosity]] rating.
# {{senseid|en|molecular weight}}{{lb|en|physics}} [[mass|Mass]] ([[atomic weight]], [[molecular weight]], etc.) {{qualifier|in restricted circumstances}}.
# {{lb|en|physics|proscribed}} {{synonym of|en|mass}} {{qualifier|in general circumstances}}.
# {{lb|en|measurement}} [[mass|Mass]] ([[net weight]], [[troy weight]], [[carat weight]], etc.).
#: {{ux|en|I'm the same '''weight''' as I was ten years ago.}}
# {{lb|en|analysis|measure theory}} {{ellipsis of|en|weight function}}.
## {{lb|en|statistics}} A [[variable]] which multiplies a value for ease of statistical [[manipulation]].
## {{lb|en|especially in|_|computing|ML}} [[emphasis|Emphasis]] applied to a given [[criterion]].
##* {{quote-av|en|year=2017|author=[https://www.youtube.com/@upandatom Up and Atom]|title=Machine Learning Explained in 5 Minutes|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3bJ7RChxMWQ|passage=Even though it's got its two features of color and hardness, it doesn't know how much importance or, as [[computer scientist]]s say, '''weight''' to place on each of them.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2024|author=Laura Masbruch|title=Pasta Land|passage=“Logits” are the [[vector]]s of '''weights'''.}}
# {{lb|en|topology}} The smallest [[cardinality]] of a [[base]].
# {{lb|en|typography}} The [[boldness]] of a [[font]]; the relative thickness of its [[stroke]]s.
#: {{coi|en|font '''weight'''}}
# {{lb|en|visual art}} The relative thickness of a drawn [[rule]] or painted [[brushstroke]], [[line weight]].
# {{lb|en|visual art}} The [[illusion]] of [[mass]].
# {{lb|en|visual art}} The [[thickness]] and [[opacity]] of [[paint]].
# The thickness of [[yarn]].
#* {{RQ:Guardian|title=How to make colourful crocheted flowers|author=Carmen Heffernan|date=August 23 2011
|text=If you'd like to use a different '''weight''' of yarn, just check the label for the recommended crochet hook size and use that.
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2011/aug/23/how-to-make-crocheted-flowers}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Spin Off|year=2026|volume=L|number=1|page=16|title=Yagaa: Reviving Sericulture in Southern Mexico|author=Elise Young
|text=The '''weight''' of the finished thread also varies with the spinner, although the general aim is laceweight singles for weaving.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[pressure|Pressure]]; [[burden]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''weight''' of care or business}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|act=V|scene=iii|page=309|column=2|passage=The '''waight''' of this ſad time we muſt obey{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=2|passage=For the public all this '''weight''' he bears.}}
# The [[resistance]] against which a [[machine]] acts, as opposed to the [[power]] which moves it.
# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} [[shipment|Shipments]] of (often illegal) [[drug]]s.
#: {{ux|en|He was pushing '''weight'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Noire Thug-A-Licious|page=103|passage=The three of us were hanging out rapping in Hamilton projects with some niggahs Pimp had got tight with on Rikers Island. Them fools had done a push-in and took over some old lady's apartment, and they were in there cutting crack and mixing '''weight'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} One [[pound]] of [[drug]]s, especially [[cannabis]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Nicholas Dorn; Karim Murji; Nigel South|title=Traffickers: Drug Markets and Law Enforcement|page=5
|passage=[I was] doing a '''weight''' [1 lb. at that time] a week, sometimes more, sometimes less.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Martina Cole|title=The Ladykiller|passage=The ones the CIB should be looking out for, to her mind, were the officers who raided a flat, found a couple of '''weights''' of cannabis and stashed half of it before they made the collar. The cannabis would make its way back on to the street {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|criminal|_|slang|dated}} [[money|Money]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1974|author=Martin R. Haskell; Lewis Yablonsky|title=Crime and Delinquency|page=96|passage=No matter how much money he makes, he is still a soldier, but he has the '''weight'''.}}
# {{lb|en|martial arts}} [[weight class|Weight class]].
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis|19|text=You’re no match for ’em. You ain’t up to their '''weight'''. It’s like little Black Strap standing up to Tom Spring,—the Black’s a pretty fighter but, Law bless you, his arm ain’t long enough to touch Tom,—and I tell you, you’re going it with fellers beyond your '''weigh'''t.}}
## {{non-gloss|Used as part of compound words for [[weight class]] titles, e.g. [[heavyweight]], [[flyweight]]}}.

